{"uid":"270c02603475c0af","name":"test_graphql_returns_errors_for_nonexistent_product_update","fullName":"tests.products.graphql.test_product_error_handling#test_graphql_returns_errors_for_nonexistent_product_update","historyId":"a603754c73ecb929f744587e82bd878a","time":{"start":1795643598432,"stop":1795643599029,"duration":597},"description":"\nVerify that updating a Product after it has been deleted returns a\nGraphQL-level error.\n\nThe test deliberately creates and then permanently deletes a real Product\nbefore attempting the update. This is deterministic and avoids relying on\nan arbitrary ID such as ``999999999`` not existing in the database.\n\nThe update request itself is valid according to the GraphQL schema, so this\nexercises resolver/business-level error handling rather than schema\nvalidation.\n\nGraphQL is expected to return HTTP 200 because the request was successfully\nprocessed at the HTTP level. The failed mutation is therefore detected by\nchecking ``response.errors`` and ``response.ok``.\n\nThe Product is explicitly deleted before the negative update, so no shared\ncleanup registration is required for this test.\n","descriptionHtml":"<p>Verify that updating a Product after it has been deleted returns a<br />\nGraphQL-level error.</p>\n<p>The test deliberately creates and then permanently deletes a real Product<br />\nbefore attempting the update. This is deterministic and avoids relying on<br />\nan arbitrary ID such as <code>999999999</code> not existing in the database.</p>\n<p>The update request itself is valid according to the GraphQL schema, so this<br />\nexercises resolver/business-level error handling rather than schema<br />\nvalidation.</p>\n<p>GraphQL is expected to return HTTP 200 because the request was successfully<br />\nprocessed at the HTTP level. The failed mutation is therefore detected by<br />\nchecking <code>response.errors</code> and <code>response.ok</code>.</p>\n<p>The Product is explicitly deleted before the negative update, so no shared<br />\ncleanup registration is required for this test.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"base_url","time":{"start":1795643591179,"stop":1795643591179,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_verify_url","time":{"start":1795643591179,"stop":1795643591180,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_session_faker","time":{"start":1795643591180,"stop":1795643591231,"duration":51},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"pytestconfig","time":{"start":1795643591231,"stop":1795643591231,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"delete_output_dir","time":{"start":1795643591231,"stop":1795643591231,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"graphql_client","time":{"start":1795643596444,"stop":1795643596444,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_pw_trace_api_requests","time":{"start":1795643598432,"stop":1795643598432,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCou